 their opening match to India and finished only ninth."] "\n\n" [:p {} "China had the same line-up as in Tokyo, including " [:a {:href "/athletes/141782"} "Chen Meng"] " and " [:a {:href "/athletes/2504735"} "Sun Yingsha"] ", the finalists in the singles, and " [:a {:href "/athletes/141783"} "Wang Manyu"] ", ranked third in the world. Asia’s dominance was even greater than in the men’s event. Six of the seven Asian teams advanced from the first round, accompanied only by Germany and Sweden from Europe."] "\n"] [:table {:class "table table-striped"} [:thead {} [:tr {} [:th {} "Pos"] [:th {} "Competitors"] [:th {} "NOC"] [:th {}] [:th {}] [:th {}]]] [:tbody {} [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "1"] [:td {} "People's Republic of China"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/CHN"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/CHN.png"}] "CHN"]] [:td {} [:span {:class "Gold"} "Gold"]] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {}] [:td {:colspan "8"} [:a {:href "/athletes/141782"} "Chen Meng"] " • " [:a {:href "/athletes/2504735"} "Sun Yingsha"] " • " [:a {:href "/athletes/141783"} "Wang Manyu"]]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "2"] [:td {} "Japan"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/JPN"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/JPN.png"}] "JPN"]] [:td {} [:span {:class "Silver"} "Silver"]] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {}] [:td {:colspan "8"} [:a {:href "/athletes/155142"} "Miwa Harimoto"] " • " [:a {:href "/athletes/155141"} "Hina Hayata"] " • " [:a {:href "/athletes/2505392"} "Miu Hirano"]]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "3"] [:td {} "Republic of Korea"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/KOR"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/KOR.png"}] "KOR"]] [:td {} [:span {:class "Bronze"} "Bronze"]] [:td {}] [:td 